## Archetype: {{project.archetype}}

{{#if (eq project.archetype "api")}}
This is a **standard API** — it owns its data, exposes HTTP endpoints, and contains full domain logic.
- Commands persist via repositories
- Queries read from repositories or read models
- Full domain model with entities, value objects, aggregates
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq project.archetype "bff-api")}}
This is a **BFF API (Backend-for-Frontend)** — it is a routing layer between a frontend and downstream services.
- **Commands dispatch to a message broker** — they do NOT persist
- **Queries call downstream REST APIs** — they do NOT access a database
- Domain layer contains **interfaces and contracts only** — no business logic execution
- **No persistence dependencies** — no repositories, no database, no ORM
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq project.archetype "microservice")}}
This is a **Microservice** — it is message-driven, owns its data, and is NOT HTTP-first.
- Commands triggered by inbound messages from a broker, not HTTP requests
- Full domain logic with persistence
- Publishes integration events for other services
- REST endpoints only for health checks or admin
{{/if}}

